# demo, the gui library's tour of 21 dialogs, each opening at 0 0 when the one before it is disposed: the Introduction's Next has the
# focus and a space takes it; the drop-down List is opened by its arrow (248 97) and green chosen; the EditList's text is made blue by keys;
# the non-editable TextList is scrolled three lines by its arrow (327 189); hello and world are typed into the editable TextList and Show
# pressed; the eye of the image buttons is pressed; on the Text Buttons screen First and the ButtonGroup's 2 are pressed. Each Next is clicked
# where its dialog puts it. The script stops there: the eighth screen, the tick() demo, writes the clock every second and never holds still,
# so the road ends the program on the Text Buttons screen (its terminal lines are withheld, as the road withholds them from a program it ends)
move 150 150
key space
wait
click 1 248 97
wait
click 1 180 140
wait
click 1 200 226
wait
click 1 230 97
key End
key BackSpace
key BackSpace
key BackSpace
type blue
wait
click 1 200 226
wait
click 1 327 189
click 1 327 189
click 1 327 189
wait
click 1 200 262
wait
click 1 200 200
type hello
key Return
type world
wait
click 1 133 349
wait
click 1 264 349
wait
click 1 200 151
move 200 270
wait
click 1 200 226
wait
click 1 100 97
wait
click 1 200 199
wait
